# endpaper workspace

This directory is an endpaper workspace: plain Markdown files with YAML frontmatter, no
database. Every command below runs non-interactively and produces stable, parseable output.

## Layout

```
.endpaper/config.toml   workspace marker, do not edit
meetings/               one markdown file per meeting
notes/                  one markdown file per typed or untyped note
notes/daily/            one markdown file per day, named YYYY-MM-DD.md
tasks.md                reserved for a future feature, currently empty
AGENTS.md               this file
```

## Frontmatter

Every file in `meetings/` and `notes/` (daily notes included) starts with exactly these six keys:

```yaml
---
id: m_20260728_a1b2c3d4
type: "standup"
title: "Q3 planning"
tags: ["platform"]
created: 2026-07-28T09:14:00
updated: 2026-07-28T09:14:00
---
```

`id` is prefixed `m_` for meetings, `n_` for notes. `type` is `""` when untyped; `tags` is `[]`.

## Commands

```bash
endpaper meeting new "Q3 planning" --type standup --tag platform
endpaper meeting list                                    # tab-separated, newest first
endpaper meeting list --json                             # array of objects, 7 keys each
endpaper meeting list --type standup --tag platform --since 2026-07-01
```

`--tag` is repeatable and is the supported way to attach tags on the command line — an
unquoted `#tag` is eaten by the shell before endpaper ever sees it. A `#tag` token inside a
*quoted* description is also parsed out, as a convenience.

Notes take the same `new`/`list` commands and flags, plus a no-argument daily note command:

```bash
endpaper note today                                      # open/create today's note
endpaper note new "vendor landscape" --type research --tag procurement
endpaper note list --json --type daily --since 2026-07-01
```

## Exit codes

`0` success · `1` not found · `2` usage error · `3` workspace error. Diagnostics go to
stderr; data goes to stdout; the two are never interleaved.
